<title>FRANCE: Cerus 1996 net attrib 1.21 profit bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>Cerus 1996 net attrib 1.21 profit bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>French holding company Cerus said on Wednesday it had net attributable profit of 1.21 billion francs in 1996.</p>
<p>It said its 1996 results were not comparable with those of 1995, since it had made significant asset sales in 1996, including the sale of its stake in car components company Valeo.</p>
<p>It made provisision in 1996 of 764 million francs, bringing total group provisions to around 1.1 billion francs.</p>
</text>
